     "text": "{\"count\":3,\"rationale\":\"Two blocks are not enough, so the minimum is 3 (for example h4_0:escalate, h4_2:pivot and h2_0:traverse). The target crown:obtain is OR, so all three of h4_0:escalate, h4_2:pivot and h4_1:reach must be made unreachable. (1) h4_0:escalate (OR) has three routes that need separate blocks: h2_0 (from edge0), h3_2 (from h2_0, h1_2 or h1_1) and h2_1 (AND of edge1, h1_0 and h1_1, all reachable). No single block other than h4_0 itself stops it. (2) h4_2:pivot (OR) has two independent routes: h2_2 (via h1_2), with h3_1 also depending on h2_2, and h3_2 (with several parents). No single block other than h4_2 itself stops it. (3) So a 2-block solution would have to be {h4_0, h4_2}. That leaves h4_1:reach (AND of h2_2 and h2_0), and both are reachable, so the target is still reachable. (4) Adding a block on h2_0 or h2_2 cuts h4_1. Blocking {h4_0, h4_2, h2_0} disables all three parents of the target.\"}"
